{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1137607-problems-with-1e-mage-shields","id":1137607,"title":"Problems with 1E Mage Shields","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-04T22:15:03-07:00","id":1137607,"title":"Problems with 1E Mage Shields","content":"I realize the mage shields in 1E were mechanically broken in some way, or the developers would not have made them into Attainments instead. It bugs me though that there is this artificial reason for damage mitigation not being a spell in a game where you are supposed to be able to accomplish anything imaginable with spells.<br /> <br /> Can someone definitely convince me it's a bad idea to let mage shields be spells and use the spellcasting rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T01:24:54-07:00","id":1137623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1137607-problems-with-1e-mage-shields#post1137607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize the mage shields in 1E were mechanically broken in some way, or the developers would not have made them into Attainments instead. It bugs me though that there is this artificial reason for damage mitigation not being a spell in a game where you are supposed to be able to accomplish anything imaginable with spells.<br /> <br /> Can someone definitely convince me it's a bad idea to let mage shields be spells and use the spellcasting rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Mage Armour right, and not the shielding practice?<br /> <br /> Spell control? Mage Armour is reflexive and cant be dispelled/countered. I dont see what advantage having mage armor as a spell could possibly provide other than possibly being able to cast it on others again. But you have the shielding practice for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 09-05-2017, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T02:34:44-07:00","id":1137631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1137607-problems-with-1e-mage-shields?p=1137623#post1137623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean Mage Armour right, and not the shielding practice?<br /> <br /> Spell control? Mage Armour is reflexive and cant be dispelled/countered. I dont see what advantage having mage armor as a spell could possibly provide other than possibly being able to cast it on others again. But you have the shielding practice for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I mean Mage Armour. Thank you for pointing it out.<br /> <br /> I can see why the players would like it as a spell rather than as an Attainment; it does not cost mana and you can use advanced Duration on it, meaning you can walk around indefinitely with mage armour. You can also increase Potency so you can have a higher Defense / Armour than your Arcana dots would limit in an Attainment.<br /> <br /> I suppose this was part of the problem in 1E, right? That players before long could sport 5/5 armours continually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T03:57:58-07:00","id":1137642,"title":"","content":"Spells can grant you almost complete immunity to stuff under their purview. They typically can't be activated Reflexively though. Mage Armor isn't a safety solution in most cases it's a panic button.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T13:56:10-07:00","id":1140003,"title":"","content":"Mage Armor is indeed the &quot;Oh shit!&quot; button. You can still create effects that shield.<br /> <br /> You can also generate barriers with appropriate Arcana, whether plant for Life, force/wind for Forces, matter for Matter, ephemera with Death, Plantonic ideals with Prime. Maybe haul in a spirit wall with Spirit, but you need prep for that. Fate can make you force people to make mistakes or other tricks, Space can say &quot;haha your attacks go this way now&quot;, Mind/Life can hide you, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}